  "content": {
    "id": "p28-q5-response",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "5",
    "prompt": "A triangle has sides of length 9 cm, 13 cm and 18 cm. Calculate the size of the largest angle, correct to one decimal place.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$108.4^\\circ$",
      "worked": "The largest angle $\\theta$ is opposite the longest side, 18 cm.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}18^2&=9^2+13^2-2\\times9\\times13\\cos\\theta\\\\\\cos\\theta&=\\frac{9^2+13^2-18^2}{2\\times9\\times13}\\\\\\cos\\theta&=-\\frac{37}{117}\\\\\\theta&=\\cos^{-1}\\left(-\\frac{37}{117}\\right)\\\\\\theta&\\approx108.4^\\circ\\end{align*}$$\n\nThe largest angle is $108.4^\\circ$, correct to one decimal place.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 40
  },
